  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">REGIONAL CAPACITY BUILDING AND KNOWLEDGE SHARING IN STRENGTHENING HEALTH SYSTEMS</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overriding goal is to support a premiere South African institution to play a leadership role in the region by assisting other countries to strengthen their health systems while addressing emerging public health problems, including the spread of drug resistant strains of tuberculosis. To this end, the project will: (i) establish regional capacity for quality assured laboratory diagnostic services, (ii) assist to put in place monitoring and evaluation capacity, and (iii) develop and oversee an operational research agenda in collaboration with other African institutions, using tuberculosis as an entry point. The development objective of this grant is to assist the Medical Research Council to build regional capacity through the transfer of knowledge and expertise in setting up quality assured TB diagnostic services in Botswana, Lesotho, Namibia and Swaziland, to deal with the threat posed by the spread of drug resistant TB in the sub-region.</narrative>
  </description>
